-- title:
--   The rebuild of a gate computes `gateApply` (`sumS_gate`)
-- statement:
--   The rebuild of a gate computes `gateApply`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6ILNet`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL.sumS_gate {v : ℕ} (g : Matrix (Fin W ⊕ Fin T) (Fin W ⊕ Fin T) (ZMod 2))
--       (S : Finset (Fin W ⊕ Fin T)) (st : Fin W ⊕ Fin T → List (ZMod 2))
--       (h : ∀ x, (st x).length = v) (n : ℕ) (hn : n < T + W) :
--       sumS (tabS st) v (srcT (ngOf g S) n) = tabS (Bit.gateApply v g S st) n
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, item language: a `QHNet` program on a table of `T + W` streams
--
--   The wires `Fin W ⊕ Fin T` of a round-six network are laid out as a table of `T + W` streams of
--   length `v` on stack `0` (temporaries first: `inr t ↦ t`, `inl w ↦ T + w`, `eqv`).
--
--   * `gateH_fsp`: a gate `(g, S)` is one fine rebuild `rebuildCU (T + W) (srcT (ngOf g S))`
--     (frozen KIL3/KFD table code), with denotation `gateApply`;
--   * `instrH`, `netH`: the code of an instruction / of a program, an edge `(x, e)` being run in
--     place by `applyCF` with an edge code `E e`;
--   * `netH_runs`: the program code computes `netRunH v impl prog` whenever every edge code
--     computes `impl e` on single streams (under the invariant `Inv G0`).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Part of the Lean formalization of the round-six κ-improvement (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign, target `IntMul.Kappa.jain_round6_framework`). The statement is copied verbatim from the Lean development; the platform node carries the same declaration name. Definitions it mentions live in the `IntMul_Kappa_R6_Defs*` bundles (on top of the published κ bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*`).
